meta {
  name: Sync
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/google-calendar/sync/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Pulls the signed-in caller's own connected Google Calendar events (next 30
  days) and desired-states them onto their AssociateAvailabilityBlock rows -
  same create_associate_availability_block()/assert_associate_block_no_overlap()
  path the manual Associate Blocks API uses (see availability/Blocks.bru),
  so an imported block still respects overlap rules and still runs exception
  detection against existing appointments.

  Only "busy" events count: events marked "free" (transparency=transparent),
  cancelled events, and events the caller declined are skipped. An all-day
  event (e.g. leave/out-of-office) is imported as a one-off block spanning
  the full day(s) it covers. A recurring Google event only
  imports as a recurring Biopeak block if its RRULE is a plain never-ending
  weekly pattern (FREQ=WEEKLY, no UNTIL/COUNT) - anything else (daily,
  monthly, a recurrence with an end) is skipped rather than approximated,
  since Biopeak recurring blocks can't express an end date.

  The caller must have an active Associate profile with at least one active
  center assignment - a block is imported once per active center they're
  assigned to (an associate's real-world "busy" applies everywhere they
  work, not just one location). Re-running this is idempotent: unchanged
  events are left alone, edited events replace their old block(s), and
  events removed from Google deactivate their previously-imported block(s).
  400s with "Connect Google Calendar before syncing." if not connected.

  Method: POST
  Path: /google-calendar/sync/
  Source: integrations.google_calendar.views.GoogleCalendarSyncView
  Auth: Admin or Associate (JWT).

  Success: {"detail": "Google Calendar sync completed.", "data": {"synced": true, "created": 0, "replaced": 0, "removed": 0, "skipped_conflicts": 0, "exception_scan": null}}
  No-op (nothing to sync into): {"data": {"synced": false, "reason": "..."}}
}
